ink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(119.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(140.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(206.5 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(240.917162 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\" d=\"M 3174 2259 Q 3174 2176 3072 2176 L 480 2170 Q 435 2170 416 2189 Q 397 2208 397 2246 L 397 2522 Q 397 2598 454 2598 L 3110 2598 Q 3174 2598 3174 2534 L 3174 2259 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(124.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(145.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(211.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(330.685173 40.193158) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(64.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\" transform=\"translate(85.8125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(149.90625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pf6f6b8a83e\"><rect x=\"35.299719\" y=\"9.768\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Annual profit impact ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>Upgraders:</b> 22.4k customers. Each moves from $6 to $11 margin a month: +$5. Annual: 22.4k × $5 × 12 = <b>$1.34M</b>.</p> <p><b>New customers:</b> 30k × $11 × 12 = <b>$3.96M</b>.</p> <p>Minus the $0.94M monitoring fee: <b>$4.36M a year</b>. The $1.3M launch cost pays back in about 4 months.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> new customers drive most of the value. If you'd counted upgraders' full premium margin you'd get $5.98M, overstating by $1.61M.</p>"},{"q":"How sensitive is this to the forecast of 30,000 new customers?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Each new customer is worth $132 a year. Without any new customers, profit would be $0.40M a year, and the launch cost would take 3.2 years to recover.</p> <p>New customers needed just to cover the monitoring fee, given the upgrades: none: upgrades alone cover it.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the plan pays even if new-customer demand disappoints, because upgrades are profitable on their own.</p>"},{"q":"What could go wrong after launch?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>False alarms</b> raising monitoring costs above $7 a month</li><li><b>Service quality</b>: slow response would damage the brand</li> <li><b>Contract terms</b>: the $0.94M minimum fee is owed even if take-up is low</li><li>Regulatory checks for monitored alarm services</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Launch the premium plan. It adds about $4.36M a year: $1.34M from upgraders (counting only their extra margin) and $3.96M from new customers, after the $0.94M monitoring fee, and repays the $1.3M launch cost in about 4 months. It remains profitable even with no new customers. Risk: false alarms push monitoring costs up, so track cost per customer monthly. Next step: agree a monitoring contract with a lower minimum fee for the first year.","great":["Counts upgraders' extra margin only","Separates one-off and recurring costs","Tests the most uncertain forecast","Flags service and cost risks"],"id":43,"slug":"elm-home-security"}